    { question: "What IBC occupancy is assisted living?", answer: "Commonly R-4 (small facilities), R-2, or I-1 for larger facilities, depending on occupant load and resident capability. Nursing is I-2. The AHJ confirms the classification for the specific project." },
    { question: "Can I design to the lighter standard to save money?", answer: "Only if the licensed population genuinely fits it. Designing a nursing-level building to board-and-care standards is a life-safety failure and a licensing violation — the savings evaporate at the first survey or incident." }
